  data: {
    LLM: 'When choosing the first foundation card, look at the reserve and choose a rank that lets you play the first reserve cards early and the last ones late.\n\nMoving cards from the reserve should be highest priority; look ahead for opportunities to move the top reserve cards and avoid plays that block them.\n\nKeep the discard pile small. Fill empty tableaus from the discard unless filling from the stock lets you immediately play a card from the discard as well. Keep as many one-card tableaus as reasonable so they can be moved to create an empty pile.',
    Player: 'When choosing the first foundation card, look at the reserve and choose a rank that lets you play the first reserve cards early and the last ones late.\n\nMoving cards from the reserve should be highest priority; look ahead for opportunities to move the top reserve cards and avoid plays that block them.\n\nKeep the discard pile small. Fill empty tableaus from the discard unless filling from the stock lets you immediately play a card from the discard as well. Keep as many one-card tableaus as reasonable so they can be moved to create an empty pile.',
